title: 5-lens audit of the Warpline replacement arc (Fable) — the keystone is fabric-schema-v2, before M1c
summary: 'A full 5-lens read-only panel (Arky/arch, Judge/review, Aegis/security, North/product, Loid/agent-moat) audited proposed-vs-built for the Warpline byte-authoritative replacement (TD-2026-07-01-263) across four vectors: AI agents, humans, cross-tree, beyond. Unanimous: the store DIRECTION and the hard part (meaning-level admission + fail-closed materialization + native object store) are SOUND and well-tested; the gaps are wiring/sequencing, not thesis failure. The convergent keystone finding: a single fabric-schema-v2 migration (A1 hash-chain + parentPickId + second merge-parent + authoredBy:agentId) simultaneously closes tamper-evidence, fixes the compounding identity-DAG debt, starts the calibration moat, and unblocks branching+M2 history — and it gets strictly more expensive with every strand sealed, so it must precede M1c cutover, reversing the checkpoint plan that had M1c next and A1 as later-optional.'
