learnings:
  - A1 (pickId hash-chain) is not just tamper-evidence — it is the same schema change that fixes the identity-DAG debt (parentPickId, two-parent merges), starts the moat (authoredBy:agentId), and unblocks branching. Doing it as one migration BEFORE more history accrues is the highest-leverage move; deferring it compounds an unauthenticatable + non-well-formed prefix that pickId immutability makes unfixable.
  - 'Confirmed real bugs beyond sequencing: (1) pick.ts:97-99 fails OPEN on an unloadable parent → seal.ts:73-74 seals an EMPTY-delta strand on the daily-driver verb (the exact silent-history-corruption class TD-263 claimed fixed — fixed in admit/fabric, NOT in pick). (2) admit.ts:256 H1 guard still refuses CLEAN admits over a merged tip even though M1b shipped the MergeRecipe that was the stated blocker → multi-agent work serializes to one merge per generation at N>=3. (3) agentId is never recorded on the strand (admit.ts:189-192) — all 14 live strands attribute to ''ascend''; the moat keys on an identity the ledger doesn''t capture. (4) snapshotDir has no ignore semantics → worktree picks ingest node_modules/.env as permanent content-addressed objects with no gc. (5) restoreTree (snapshot.ts:179) has no path-traversal/symlink guard — CVE-2021-21300 class, ships as an exploit primitive when M1c lands restore as a verb.'
  - 'Strategy (North+Loid concur): replacement stays the quiet north star, but the SHIPPABLE product today is mirror-mode + the trojan-horse ''Warpline Guard'' (oracle/lifeline/grade packaged as a zero-config CI check on plain git+TS repos, no Paradigm init). lifeline (rename-surviving blame) is the one verb already better than git today. GAP-1 (non-symbol files invisible to `warpline status`) is the trust-killer and has no milestone.'
  - 'M1 is NOT actually complete: restore is a library primitive only (no `warpline restore` verb), backfill is unbuilt, so ''reconstruct with git absent'' is true of a fixture, not of any real repo''s pre-M1b history. Do not claim M1 done before the restore verb + A4 cutover-refusal + ignore semantics + a rehydrate path exist.'
